Answer in plain text, nothing else and no code fence: a line "Complexity: " with simple, moderate or complex; a line "Epics: " with a whole number, 1 or more; then a blank line and one sentence explaining the classification.

How to fill it:
- Complexity: simple is a single product with a clear scope and one or two kinds of users; moderate has several kinds of users, a moderate feature set and some integrations; complex is an enterprise product with many kinds of users, deep integrations, regulation or several teams.
- Epics: the epics the whole product needs, sized to the brief, not to a habit.

